Starting this file to follow the dev on my ft_traceroute and help me clear my mind when having to reflect on what to do.

Traceroute is an utility that let you route the path a packet take to the target host.
Looking into how it works I realised that I could reuse a good part of my ft_ping since they both uses ICMP packet and raw socket.

So to clarify what I have and what I need to change I'll write them as a reference. Then I'll write a list of the first things I'll need to do.

What I have that will be useful for ft_traceroute:
	-complete raw socket setup
	-target host argument
	-packet rx tx
	-response parsing
	-sending loop
	-error handling
	-Display functions
	-Headers with stats

What I need to change for ft_traceroute:
	-Only need one argument for target host
	-Change sending loop to send 3 packets at once and increment ttl (which start at 1)
	-Change and find a solution to save stats for 3 packets
	-Change loop condition to break when ECHO_REPLY is received
	-Change display functions to match traceroute display

What I should do to start:
	-Change the Makefile and rename files if need be
	-Start by changing the header file so then I can make the changes by correcting the compiler errors.
	-Correct the main file so it take the right argument and right option
	-Change the ttl before sending
	-Correct the sending loop break condition and packets sent

