Modifying the structure, the logic and reading the man traceroute made me understand that I'll need to use some sort of timeout mechanic. But I still don't really know if I need to calculate checksum for each probe.

The idea for the loop is:
	-send a probe with ttl=1
	-wait for reply under timeout value
	-if timeout -> print "*" and continue
	-if reply, save rtt in array and continue
	-when 3 rtt are saved increment ttl and go again
I'm not sure if icmp sequence is relevant in traceroute

